---
import BlogLayout from "../../layouts/BlogLayout.astro";
import { posts } from "../../data/blog";
import { profile } from "../../data/profile";
const post = posts.find(
  (p) => p.slug === "apple-design-award-finalist-wwdc26",
)!;
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<BlogLayout
  title={`${post.title}, Lilly Seay`}
  description={post.description}
  image={post.cover}
>
  <article class="post prose-post">
    <header class="post-head wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">
        Blog · Apple Design Awards 2026 and WWDC26, as I posted it
      </p>
      <h1>{post.title}</h1>
      <p class="post-meta">
        By {profile.name} · {post.date} · {post.readTime}
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="wrap post-body">
      <figure class="li-embed">
        <iframe
          src="https://www.linkedin.com/embed/feed/update/urn:li:ugcPost:7471272537973252096?compact=1"
          height="399"
          width="504"
          frameborder="0"
          allowfullscreen=""
          title="WWDC26 vlog as an Apple Design Award finalist, embedded from LinkedIn"
        ></iframe>
        <figcaption>
          My WWDC26 vlog as an Apple Design Award finalist.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h2>The announcement</h2>
      <div class="post-entry">
        <p class="eyebrow">
          May 2026 · <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7462194542281142272/"
            >on LinkedIn</a
          >
        </p>
        <p>
          My app Hearing Buddy is an Apple Design Award Finalist in Inclusivity!
          🎉🦻🌈 This is a dream I’ve had for the last decade of designing apps.
          What’s most special to me is that Hearing Buddy is a finalist in
          Inclusivity. As a disabled female founder, inclusivity and
          accessibility are the backbone of everything I do. The Hearing Buddy
          brand is a colorful expression of my disability pride and commitment
          to making hearing solutions accessible to all. Lastly, going through
          my hearing loss journey with my real-life Hearing Buddy Scott Krager,
          building an app together, and now being Apple Design Award Finalists
          together is bittersweet. He’s my biggest supporter in all aspects of
          my life. Cheers to my best Liquid Glass designs yet. I put my heart
          and soul into the UI/UX. (Download the app, and let me know what you
          think of my designs🩵💙) Thank you to my partnership manager
          Christopher Tan and everyone at Apple that has rooted for Hearing
          Buddy! I wouldn’t be here without you👏 We will be at WWDC26!!!!!! I’m
          so excited to go with Scott. Now, time to celebrate!!🥳
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="post-figure">
        <img
          src={`${base}/blog/wwdc26/../top-linkedin-posts/02-ada-finalist.jpg`}
          alt="Apple Design Awards 2026 finalist graphic for Hearing Buddy"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>Apple Design Awards 2026 finalist, Inclusivity.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="post-entry">
        <p class="eyebrow">
          June 2026 · <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7467948824699850752/"
            >on LinkedIn</a
          >
        </p>
        <p>
          A huge congratulations to Guitar Wiz for winning an Apple Design Award
          in Inclusivity! 🎉👏
        </p>
      </div>
      <h2>Getting to Cupertino</h2>
      <div class="post-entry">
        <p class="eyebrow">
          June 2026 · <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7468819513220743168/"
            >on LinkedIn</a
          >
        </p>
        <p>
          Officially in Cupertino for WWDC26!! I’m soooo excited to go as an ADA
          finalist. Of course, I had to take a Waymo🔥
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="post-entry">
        <p class="eyebrow">
          June 2026 · <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7469474755620917248/"
            >on LinkedIn</a
          >
        </p>
        <p>
          Picking up my badge in a few hours!! Can’t wait to see the WWDC26
          swag😍
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="post-figure">
        <img
          src={`${base}/blog/wwdc26/hello-selfie.jpg`}
          alt="Lilly and Scott in front of the hello sculpture at the Apple Developer Center"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>Badge pickup at the Developer Center.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h2>WWDC26</h2>
      <div class="post-entry">
        <p class="eyebrow">
          June 2026 · <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7469759272524910592/"
            >on LinkedIn</a
          >
        </p>
        <p>We are at WWDC26 today!!! 🎉🔥</p>
      </div>
      <div class="post-entry">
        <p class="eyebrow">
          June 2026 · <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7469837105968435201/"
            >on LinkedIn</a
          >
        </p>
        <p>
          All of the ADA Finalists and Winners at the WWDC26 badge event
          yesterday!🎉 so much excellence in one photo👏 We got to showcase
          Hearing Buddy and talk to a bunch of people!! I’ve loved sharing how
          Apple’s latest technologies have changed my life if the most positive
          way by helping me hear better in conversations. Of course, I take a
          pic with the ADA award every time I go to WWDC. It’s my dream to win
          one🥹 Apple had a wonderful reception for all the ADA finalists. I had
          so much fun yesterday with Scott Krager! Apple really thought through
          every detail to make our ADA WWDC experience special. More to come on
          what WWDC26 announcements were my fave and what we will be integrating
          into Hearing Buddy! 🙂
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="post-figure">
        <img
          src={`${base}/blog/wwdc26/finalists-group.jpg`}
          alt="The 2026 Apple Design Award finalists and winners gathered around the WWDC26 sign at Apple Park"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>
          All of the Apple Design Award finalists and winners at the WWDC26
          badge event.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="post-figure two">
        <div>
          <img
            src={`${base}/blog/wwdc26/caption-with-pride.jpg`}
            alt="Lilly and two friends in caption with pride shirts"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <img
            src={`${base}/blog/wwdc26/showing-hearing-buddy.jpg`}
            alt="Lilly holding up Hearing Buddy on her iPhone"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
        <figcaption>Showing Hearing Buddy at Apple Park.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="video-figure small">
        <video
          controls
          playsinline
          preload="metadata"
          poster={`${base}/blog/wwdc26/inclusivity-display-poster.jpg`}
        >
          <source
            src={`${base}/blog/wwdc26/inclusivity-display.mp4`}
            type="video/mp4"
          />
        </video>
        <figcaption>
          Hearing Buddy on the Inclusivity finalists display at WWDC26.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
      <div class="post-entry">
        <p class="eyebrow">
          June 2026 · <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7470243318669447168/"
            >on LinkedIn</a
          >
        </p>
        <p>
          WWDC26 was so fun! I can’t believe the Hearing Buddy logo was in the
          State of the Union😍🦻 A few things I REALLY loved: 1️⃣ Apple
          Intelligence, SiriAI, and CoreAI. We are following Apple’s lead in the
          AI space and cannot wait to use these in Hearing Buddy! 2️⃣ Child
          Safety Features, which would help us to make a version of Hearing
          Buddy for kids🥹 3️⃣ Liquid Glass improvements. We’ve got a Hearing
          Buddy build in iOS27 and no coding needed to see a difference! I’m
          very impressed at Apple’s dedication to taking feedback from
          developers and making awesome improvements. We can’t wait to start
          coding iOS27 features😏 and dive even deeper into our Liquid Glass
          designs! What was your fave WWDC26 announcement?
        </p>
      </div>
      <h2>The Observatory</h2>
      <div class="post-entry">
        <p class="eyebrow">
          June 2026 · <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7470542551654195200/"
            >on LinkedIn</a
          >
        </p>
        <p>
          A peak WWDC26 experience was demoing Hearing Buddy in The Observatory
          at Apple Park😍 It’s the most beautiful architecture I’ve ever
          experienced! We also met the founding team of Tiimo, who won App of
          the Year in 2025💅👑 It’s been the best week ever!
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure class="post-figure">
        <img
          src={`${base}/blog/wwdc26/developer-center-table.jpg`}
          alt="Lilly at a table at Apple Park with her phone"
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>Between demos at Apple Park.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <h2>The vlog</h2>
      <div class="post-entry">
        <p class="eyebrow">
          June 2026 · <a
            href="https://www.linkedin.com/feed/update/urn:li:activity:7471272647054606336/"
            >on LinkedIn</a
          >
        </p>
        <p>WWDC26 Vlog as an ADA Finalist😍👏</p>
      </div>

      <section class="post-outro reveal">
        <h2>Apple's 2026 Apple Design Awards</h2>
        <p>
          Hearing Buddy is listed as a finalist in the Inclusivity category on
          <a href="https://developer.apple.com/design/awards/"
            >Apple's Design Awards page</a
          >, in
          <a
            href="https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2026/06/apple-reveals-winners-of-the-2026-apple-design-awards/"
            >Apple's newsroom announcement of the 2026 winners</a
          >, and in the App Store story
          <a href="https://apps.apple.com/us/iphone/story/id1896567319"
            >Meet the 2026 Apple Design Award Finalists</a
          >. Apple's description: "Created by a solo developer with hearing
          loss, Hearing Buddy is shaped by experience. The thoughtful app uses
          the Foundation Models framework and on-device speech-to-text features
          to quickly generate real-time captions and summaries of spoken
          conversations."
        </p>
        <p>
          Building something for the App Store and want it to stand out? <a
            href={`mailto:${profile.email}`}>Send me a note</a
          >.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</BlogLayout>
